<article class="env-example" id="02HZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02HZ">Example <span data-tag="02HZ">5.9.5</span>.</a> Any nonempty, Kolmogorov Noetherian topological space has a closed point (combine Lemmas <a href="/tag/005E" data-tag="005E">5.12.8</a> and <a href="/tag/04ZA" data-tag="04ZA">5.12.13</a>). Let $X = \{ 1, 2, 3, \ldots \} $. Define a topology on $X$ with opens $\emptyset $, $\{ 1, 2, \ldots , n\} $, $n \geq 1$ and $X$. Thus $X$ is a locally Noetherian topological space, without any closed points. This space cannot be the underlying topological space of a locally Noetherian scheme, see Properties, Lemma <a href="/tag/02IL" data-tag="02IL">28.5.9</a>. </p>
</article>